      "geometry": "rect",
      "text": "Integration Challenge : Most studies focus either on sentiment analysis or sales forecasting, but not both together in a unified framework . Lack of integration leads to incomplete understanding of how customer opinions + engagement patterns drive sales .\n\nLimited Multi-Modal Analysis :Social media data includes text (reviews, comments), images (product photos, ads), and engagement metrics (likes, shares).Existing models usually handle only one data type, reducing prediction accuracy.\n\nReal-Time Decision Making Gap:Current models often analyze data in batches (offline), not in real-time . Marketers need instant insights during campaigns to adjust strategies dynamically.\n\nExplainability & Trust Deficit :Deep learning models (LSTM, BiLSTM) provide accurate predictions but function as a black box.Without clear explanation of feature contributions, businesses hesitate to adopt them. \n\nScalability & Resource Constraints : Complex hybrid models (e.g., GCN + LSTM + Attention) are powerful but computationally expensive, making them impractical for SMEs and startups.",
